+## 11. Scope, failed shortcuts and selected evidence
 
 The construction supplies an approximate complete preparation map to auxiliary vacuum and a prescribed computable one-excitation clock packet, with actual H0 aging, no discarded output and a finite positive local control schedule. It resolves the aged-clock input obstruction conditionally by actively resetting and synthesizing X, not by claiming the preceding auxiliary-only theorem already did so. The original clock's arbitrary information remains in E.
 
 This does not establish native pure-memory supply, gate/control manufacture, common strength caps, saturated-pair availability, the full preparation program, or an accepted simulator theorem. Full simultaneous-axis interaction simulation remains a dependency of later use, not of the literal reset/synthesis algebra. One can prepare a packet without having proved that the subsequent installed simulator implements the intended program.
 
+For later composition, the ideal starting state is the complete output (13), with D already aged by H0 for T and the displaced S records retained as part of its reference/output. If a separate full-output simulator theorem applies to that ready state under the same installed post-generator, subsequent common evolution propagates the preparation error by trace-norm contraction and its own error can be added. This does not require the actual faulty output to lie exactly in N_X=1. A theorem for nominal K cannot silently be applied to a different K_base; its static discrepancy needs the corresponding subsequent full-space error allowance. No conclusion about that separate theorem's acceptance is supplied here.
+
 Failed shortcuts are explicit: direct fresh matching at a saturated auxiliary vertex; forward-only routing; one-excitation SWAP substituted on arbitrary qubits; assuming clean old X; resetting X while leaving K_X uncompensated without a residual bound; deleting the finite release term or its K_X/S_X covariance; dividing by zero amplitudes; dropping positive-control scalar offsets; treating fresh coordinates as an induced interaction graph; recycling information-bearing E. None of these failures is a broad no-go.
 
-One selected exact diagnostic is proposed in SELECTED_PLAN.md. It will use the saved base coordinate input without rerunning its inverse or dynamics. It will check one finite routed layout and one complex four-clock synthesis identity, including zero amplitude, negative real coefficient, imaginary coefficient and final phase. The uniform geometry family, full-output Duhamel argument, source positivity and control suppliers remain analytic obligations for independent review. No numerical large-Hilbert dynamics is claimed.
+Bounded theorem: under the finite local Hamiltonian, connected routing graph, independent pure-memory and supplied-control hypotheses above, every computable normalized one-excitation packet has the finite synthesis (7)-(10). For every input (1), finite positive ramps and pulses implement the complete target (13) with (15), while returning to the declared actual installed baseline. Given a positive nominal trace tolerance e, for example r_on=e/[2(B+1)] and r_off=e/[2(Gamma+1)] make the two nominal ramp allowances sum to less than e; any positive finite pulse durations are allowed and have the prices (24)-(26). All original nonclock factors undergo actual H0 aging for the resulting T. This is an approximation theorem for readiness at a physical endpoint, with consumed supplied memory, not an exact dissipative reset or an efficient native preparation theorem.
+
+The one predeclared diagnostic in SELECTED_PLAN.md ran once at 13:32:57 UTC, with contemporaneous code/source preservation and launch receipt. It used the saved base coordinates without rerunning their inverse or dynamics. The selected layout has 70 original nonclock factors, 4 original clock factors, 121 auxiliaries and 125 new memory factors: 320 total. Its root-distance sum is 2153, giving P=19931 full SWAPs. All intermediate restoration checks and final tensor-factor permutation checks passed. The complete selected geometry has 307 NN pairs touching S/E, 271 declared and 36 omitted. Exactly one omitted edge touches the new ray, as (22) predicts; all 35 preexisting omitted edges remain in the inventory.
+
+The rational four-clock target [0,3i/5,-12/25,(48+64i)/125] is exactly normalized and the three positive pair logarithms plus pivot phase reproduce it exactly, after retaining the symbolic global phase exp(-i Theta). Exact four-by-four principal minors check positivity for these selected logarithms, and exact spectral-projector identities check full SWAP and excitation phases. The 31 named predicates are selected evidence, not independent theorem acceptance. The forward-only first routing-word mutant leaves 21 incorrect final labels; reversing the hopping sign gives squared target-vector error 1924/625. These are actual failed routes preserved in EXACT_RESULT.json.
+
+The uniform geometry family, full-output Duhamel argument, general packet synthesis, source positivity and control suppliers remain analytic claims for independent review. No waveform execution, arbitrary-H dynamics, large Hilbert matrix or new inverse was computed. The complete selected adjacency inventory and gate/path certificate are saved. Post-run analytic clarifications and actual evidence are recorded by a full diff against the contemporaneous preexecution derivation; no scientific code or input was changed or rerun.
